{
  "area": "bundle",
  "description": "AGSC-01-18 as amended for 1.1: the keys 1.1 adds are all OPTIONAL and the configuration stays closed. Derivation, case by case, each configuration being otherwise minimal and valid. (1) every key 1.1 adds, with a value of the right type, is accepted with no finding: compose.brief, discovery.ai_catalog, lint.min_sources, site.query_page, site.author_orcid, bundle.creator, bundle.license_url, contribute[].repository and branch, a typed peer of each relationship, ledger.actors and the four members of domain. The configuration declares 1.0.0, the tool's own version, so no newer-MINOR warning is raised; a Bundle that uses the keys SHOULD declare 1.1.0 or later but need not for this case. (2) a boolean given as a string is a schema failure, AGSC-E201, at compose.brief; (3) a negative lint.min_sources is AGSC-E201; (4) a string for site.query_page is AGSC-E201; (5) a relationship outside the three is a value outside an enumeration, AGSC-E203, which the precedence paragraph of spec/09 section 9.4 gives to every enumeration violation; (6) a translation-layer peer with no crosswalk lacks a required member, AGSC-E202 (AGSC-11-24); (7) a domain path with a parent-directory segment fails the relative-path grammar, a pattern violation, AGSC-E204. Exit 0 for the accepted configuration and 1 for the others: none of these is a usage-class code (AGSC-09-08).",
  "expected": {
    "cases": [
      {
        "accepted": true,
        "exit": 0,
        "findings": [],
        "name": "new-keys-accepted"
      },
      {
        "accepted": false,
        "exit": 1,
        "findings": [
          {
            "code": "AGSC-E201",
            "path": "compose.brief",
            "severity": "error"
          }
        ],
        "name": "brief-wrong-type"
      },
      {
        "accepted": false,
        "exit": 1,
        "findings": [
          {
            "code": "AGSC-E201",
